# The bundled agent-catalog prompts and manifests are hashed as LF in
# manifest.json (see agent_catalog::resolve_prompt). Windows checks out CRLF
# by default, which flips those bytes and breaks the hash check — pin them to
# LF on every platform so the on-disk content matches the recorded hash.
src-tauri/resources/agent-catalogs/** text eol=lf

# The bundled plugin-creator skill is byte-compared against the generator
# output (creator-skill-docs.test.ts) and its frontmatter is parsed with a
# literal `\n` by the CLI. A CRLF checkout breaks both — pin to LF everywhere.
src-tauri/resources/skills/** text eol=lf
